{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cdqf9ttgP6KdYEhX6j9Tk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Provenance\n\nOn 2026-07-19, a production deploy served stale artifacts due to insufficient cache-key specificity (Source 2, 14:02–14:07). The deploy-staging job had restored a cache entry keyed only on branch name, failing to account for changes to the lockfile (Source 2, 14:07). Investigation identified the cache step as the root cause, and adding the lockfile hash to the cache key resolved the issue (Source 2, 14:31). The incident consumed approximately 40 minutes of oncall time before resolution (Source 1; Source 2, 14:44). This was the first observed occurrence of this particular failure mode in the deployment pipeline (Source 2, 14:44)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":364,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":168,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
